cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Auralloy in research, please cite the software and the preprint."
type: software
title: "Auralloy: Rule-Grounded, Explainable Multi-Song Mashup Generation with an Editable Stem Timeline"
abstract: >-
  Auralloy is an open-source desktop studio for rule-based automatic mashups
  (sequential and layered), slowed + reverb and lofi, with a multi-track
  timeline editor. Every arrangement decision follows a written rule and is
  logged in plain language.
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/thecmjhb/Auralloy"
url: "https://github.com/thecmjhb/Auralloy"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hossain Bappy"
    given-names: "C. M. Jubayer"
keywords:
  - music information retrieval
  - mashup
  - beat tracking
  - key detection
  - time-stretching
  - audio effects
  - JUCE
  - explainable
